5. Energy, Thermal, and Resource Modeling

5.1 Power balance (discrete-time)

Let E_t be stored energy (battery), P_{gen} generated, P_{load} consumed:
E_{t+1} = E_t + \Delta t\left(\eta_c P_{gen,t} - \frac{1}{\eta_d}P_{load,t}\right)
Constraints:
E_{min}\le E_t \le E_{max},\quad
0\le P_{gen,t}\le P_{gen,max},\quad
0\le P_{load,t}\le P_{load,max}

5.2 Thermal network model

Let T_t \in \mathbb{R}^k be component temperatures:
T_{t+1} = AT_t + B q_t + C T_{env,t}
   •   q_t: heat inputs (electronics, heaters)
   •   T_{env}: external boundary temps / radiative sink

Safety bounds:
T_{min}\le T_t \le T_{max}

5.3 Joint energy–thermal scheduling (MPC)

\min_{U}\sum_{t=0}^{T}\left(\alpha \|T_t-T^\*\|_2^2 + \beta P_{load,t} + \rho \,Risk(x_t)\right)
Subject to the energy and thermal constraints above plus mission constraints.

