6. Fault Detection, Isolation, and Recovery (FDIR)

6.1 Residual-based detection

Define residual:
r_t = y_t - h(\hat{x}_{t|t-1})
Trigger if:
\|r_t\|_{\Sigma^{-1}}^2 > \tau

6.2 Mode switching with hybrid automata

Model system modes m \in \mathcal{M} (nominal, degraded, safe-mode, recovery):
(x,m) \xrightarrow{\text{guard}(x,y)} (x',m')
Recovery actions are policies conditioned on mode:
u_t = \pi_{m}(b_t)

6.3 Reliability objective (mission survivability)

Maximize probability of mission success:
\max_{\pi}\ \mathbb{P}_\pi(\text{Complete mission} \mid x_0)
or minimize expected downtime / risk.

