7. Governance, Authorization, and Auditability Constraints

Q-HISS autonomy is bounded by policy + authority tokens.

7.1 Governed action set

Partition actions:
   •   u \in \mathcal{U}_{free}: allowed without authorization (thermal balancing, routine scheduling)
   •   u \in \mathcal{U}_{auth}: requires authorization (high-risk maneuvers, irreversible actions)

Enforce:
u_t \in \mathcal{U}_{free}\ \cup\ \left(\mathcal{U}_{auth}\cap \mathbb{I}[\text{AuthToken}_t=1]\right)

7.2 Policy constraints as temporal logic (optional formalization)

Let mission safety rules be expressed in LTL:
\mathbf{G}(\text{TempSafe}) \wedge \mathbf{G}(\text{EnergySafe}) \wedge \mathbf{G}(\neg \text{UnsafeMode})
Controller must satisfy:
\pi \models \varphi

7.3 Tamper-evident audit log

Every decision emits an event:
e_t = (t, \hat{x}_t, u_t, m_t, \text{policy\_id}, \text{auth\_hash})
Append-only chain:
H_t = \text{Hash}(H_{t-1}\ \| \ e_t)
This supports traceability and post-mission verification.

